WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Hi, everybody.

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.268 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:05.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you guys want
to play this?

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:07.640 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You know, I feel like --

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.543
I've been thinking a lot
about life and death, you know?

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.212 line:92%
My buddy believes in heaven.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:14.481
And I asked him what his idea
of heaven was, and he said,

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:17.450
"When I die,
I believe that I'll be reunited

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:20.086 align:start size:94% position:6%
for eternity
with all of my family

00:00:20.086 --> 00:00:21.654 line:92%
that passed away before me."

00:00:21.654 --> 00:00:24.758 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought,
"Is that what we want?"

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:25.291 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:28.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you want to be reunited
with your family for eternity?

00:00:28.361 --> 00:00:31.731
If I die right now and see
my whole family on a cloud

00:00:31.731 --> 00:00:33.166 line:92%
and they're like, "Hey, Dov."

00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:34.868 line:92%
I'd be like, "Yeah, hey!"

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.237 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:37.237 --> 00:00:38.905 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll stop by and all,
you know,

00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:40.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm not doing eternity
over there.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.108 line:92%
I mean, I think we can all agree

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:46.913
the last 30 Thanksgivings have
not gone smoothly, you know?

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:47.480 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't know.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
The point is,
I can't satisfy a woman.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:52.218 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:55.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been --
I've been married.

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.223 line:92%
I'm married two years now,

00:00:57.223 --> 00:01:00.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm in couples therapy
with my wife.

00:01:00.126 --> 00:01:01.461 line:92%
And I love her very much,

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:03.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I'm still trying
to figure out

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.565 line:92%
how to talk to her, you know,

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.833 line:92%
and, like, how to communicate.

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:09.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
My wife comes
from a small town in Canada,

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:12.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
and she tends to be
a little under-expressive,

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:13.473 line:92%
a little passive aggressive,

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:16.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I tend to maybe
say too much, you know?

00:01:16.276 --> 00:01:19.145 line:92%
But if I'm wrong, correct me!

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.014 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you're wrong,
let me correct you!

00:01:21.014 --> 00:01:23.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a better life that way,
you know?

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:24.517 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I'm driving.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.685 line:92%
I'm driving near a beach,

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my wife points
in the distance.

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:30.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said,
"Look at that lifehouse."

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:31.157 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Lifehouse, with an "F."

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:33.393
Apparently, she's been under
the impression her whole life

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.728 align:start size:94% position:6%
that a lighthouse is called
a lifehouse.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:36.729 line:92%
And so I said -- I said --

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:38.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
All I said is,
"That's a lighthouse."

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said,
"That's what I said."

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:44.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said [Clears throat]
"No. You know, that --

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:45.572 size:84% position:42% line:92%
that's not what you s--

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
You said lifehouse
with an "F," you know?"

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.244 size:84% position:42%
And then you could feel
a cold, Canadian wind

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.445 size:78% position:39% line:92%
blow through the car.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:53.379 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:57.250 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she goes -- she goes,
"Well, you know everything."

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:00.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"I, you know, I mean --

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:00.753 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Clears throat ]

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:03.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
Honey, I don't know every --
I mean [Clears throat]

00:02:03.957 --> 00:02:04.958 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I know this," you know?

00:02:04.958 --> 00:02:07.527 align:start size:94% position:6%
What am I, making --
What's it? An ego thing?

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:08.628 line:92%
I know the name of the object.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:12.665
I'm not trying to make
a big deal out of it, you know?

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then I reali--
I reali--

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:16.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
since I've been in therapy

00:02:16.069 --> 00:02:19.439
and I'm getting all there
hopefully psychologically,

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:23.343
you know, I realize I don't have
to argue about every instance.

00:02:23.343 --> 00:02:27.280
And so, I just took a deep
breath and said, "Okay,"

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.215 line:92%
and I kept driving, you know?

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:30.517 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I was proud of myself.

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.385 size:88% position:44%
I then we were pulling
into the hotel at night,

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:35.989
and I stayed with the breathing
and I just put my hand on hers

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:39.225
and I just said -- I just said,
"Honey, I mean -- I mean,

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's got a damn light on it,
you know?"

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:42.829 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Like, I don't want to --

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:45.098 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:45.798 size:78% position:39% line:92%
You know what I mean?

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.834 size:81% position:41%
I'm not trying to make
a big deal out of it.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm just saying.
[ Clears throat ]

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:50.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I mean,
I don't want to argue.

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.906
I'd rather get a divorce
than call it a lifehouse,

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I don't want to argue,
you know?

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:57.544 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:01.247 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that happened --
that happened on a Friday.

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:05.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then on Monday,
we walk in to couples therapy,

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:08.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I didn't realize
my wife was still holding on

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.123 line:92%
to all of that energy, and I --

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:12.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
The way couples therapy works
is you walk in,

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.994 size:84% position:42%
and the therapist says,
"How is everything?"

00:03:14.994 --> 00:03:17.330 align:start size:94% position:6%
And before I had a chance
to sit down,

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.765 size:84% position:42% line:92%
my wife goes [Whimpers]

00:03:18.765 --> 00:03:22.535
and she goes, "I-I said
lifehouse, and he flipped out."

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.871
And I said, "That's not an
accurate characterization

00:03:24.871 --> 00:03:25.505 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
of what happened."

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:27.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said, "She did say
'lifehouse,'

00:03:27.574 --> 00:03:29.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I said, you know,
the word --

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.778 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tell her the word," you know?
"It's lighthouse!

00:03:31.778 --> 00:03:33.046 line:92%
If you could tell it to my wife,

00:03:33.046 --> 00:03:34.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
we could move on
with our lives!"

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
What's this?
A couples-therapy issue?

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's reality!
It's just a word, right?"

00:03:38.851 --> 00:03:40.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the therapist
won't say anything.

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's looking for something
deeper and he said,

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:44.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
"This seems
really important to you."

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.426 size:75% position:38%
And then I was like,
"I don't know, man.

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:47.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, important,
not important.

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
we have words for things."

00:03:49.529 --> 00:03:51.331 align:start size:94% position:6%
I always thought
the idea of a society

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:52.966 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that there's some
shared language.

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:55.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
Otherwise,
we're all pointing at objects,

00:03:55.034 --> 00:03:56.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
making up our own term,
you know?

00:03:56.936 --> 00:03:58.004 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And that would be chaos!

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:01.708
My wife is tearing down society,
you understand?

00:04:01.708 --> 00:04:04.377 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:12.185
So then -- No, I appreciate it,
but it's like --

00:04:12.185 --> 00:04:13.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we leave therapy.
You know?

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:17.690
It's going okay, our life
for the next 20 minutes.

00:04:17.690 --> 00:04:18.891 line:92%
And we stop at a coffee shop

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:21.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
and my wife is looking through
her Instagram.

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:22.996 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And it occurred to me,

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:25.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
Instagram is making
everybody's life

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:26.332 line:92%
a little bit worse, you know?

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:31.904
Because there's no way you can
feel as good about your life

00:04:31.904 --> 00:04:33.640 align:start size:94% position:6%
when comparing it to an
Instagram.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:36.776
Like, because Instagram's
not a life, it's a moment.

00:04:36.776 --> 00:04:39.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's a snapshot of a moment
from a life.

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:42.048 line:92%
It's a commercial for a life.

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.751 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you would have seen
my wife's Instagram

00:04:44.751 --> 00:04:45.918 line:92%
from our terrible weekend,

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:48.988
you would have thought we were
the Kennedys on summer break.

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:52.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
The sun is in the right place,
my wife is sipping a wine.

00:04:52.492 --> 00:04:54.494 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a --
She's got a heel up.

00:04:54.494 --> 00:04:57.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a dog catching
a Frisbee midair.

00:04:57.096 --> 00:05:00.600
There's no picture of us
having a divorce-level argument

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.535 size:88% position:44% line:92%
over a stupid lifehouse!

00:05:02.535 --> 00:05:03.503 line:92%
Have a good night, everybody.

00:05:03.503 --> 00:05:05.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you for listening.
God bless.

00:05:05.638 --> 00:05:09.309 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, my goodness!

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:13.479 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Oh!

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.715 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Dov Davidoff, everybody!

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:19.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
